---
### [INVARIANTS]
invariants:
  - "Every cartridge.json validates strictly against schemas/cartridge-v1.json; the CI gate (cartridge-schema) blocks merges on any violation"
  - "schemas/cartridge-v1.json content-SHA-256 matches schemas/PINNED-SHA; CI fails loudly on silent drift"
  - "Cartridges live under cartridges/domains/<domain>/, cartridges/cross-cutting/<category>/, or cartridges/templates/"
  - "Cartridge names end in a canonical role suffix"
  - "Leaf cartridge ABIs are axiom-free: zero believe_me / assert_total / assert_smaller / idris_crash / sorry outside comments (scripts/check-trusted-base.sh; sanctioned count here is 0, unlike boj-server's 5)"
  - "No V-language sources anywhere under cartridges/ (V banned estate-wide 2026-04-10; Zig is its replacement, not its casualty)"

shim_invariant:
  # RESTATED 2026-08-07. The previous wording — "Cartridges with a Zig FFI
  # carry their own cartridge_shim.zig beside ffi/build.zig" — was FALSE as
  # a universal. Stated here as a rule plus its recorded exceptions.
  rule: "A cartridge with a Zig FFI SHOULD carry its own cartridge_shim.zig beside ffi/build.zig, byte-identical to shim_canon. The shim is vendored by copy rather than shared because a fetched cartridge must build standalone in a flat host cache with no sibling paths to reach for."
  holds_for: 116
  exceptions:
    - path: "cartridges/domains/languages/007-mcp/ffi"
      kind: "ffi/build.zig present, no cartridge_shim.zig beside it"
    - path: "cartridges/domains/knowledge/librarian-mcp/ffi"
      kind: "ffi/build.zig present, no cartridge_shim.zig anywhere in the cartridge"
    - path: "cartridges/domains/languages/orchestrator-lsp-mcp/ffi/zig"
      kind: "build graph nested at ffi/zig/build.zig rather than ffi/build.zig; no shim at all. Not counted in ffi_build_zig above."
    - path: "cartridges/domains/gaming/npc-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig"
      kind: "shim present but NOT byte-identical to shim_canon; cause unrecorded"
  enforcement: "NONE on main. No CI job compares the copies. Open PR #109 proposes tools/sync_cartridge_shim.sh (stamp + --check) and a shim-drift job; see [PENDING] below."

---
### [CI_GATES]
# Every workflow in .github/workflows/ that is tracked in git, with its
# real gating strength. 'advisory' means findings never fail the job —
# a green check there means the tool RAN, not that the repo is clean.
ci_gates:
  - id: "cartridge-schema"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/cartridge-schema.yml"
    job: "validate"
    gating: "hard"
    mode: "strict"
    flipped_to_strict_at: "2026-06-01"
    baseline: "142 total / 142 passing / 0 failing"
    baseline_verified_at: "2026-08-07"
    baseline_command: "cd tools/validate-cartridges && deno task audit"
    note: "Also re-verifies the schema mirror SHA-256 against schemas/PINNED-SHA before validating, and runs the validator's own unit tests."
  - id: "proofs"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/proofs.yml"
    jobs: ["changes", "trusted-base", "typecheck"]
    gating: "hard"
    note: "Idris2 0.8.0 per .tool-versions. typecheck runs `idris2 --check` on each .idr INDIVIDUALLY from its abi/ root, so a stale .ipkg cannot mask a rotted module, and carries a vacuous-pass guard (PASS=0 is FAILURE). Added after 23 proofs here rotted while their boj-server twins stayed green (#36/#37)."
  - id: "zig-test"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/zig-test.yml"
    jobs: ["changes", "zig-test"]
    gating: "partial"
    note: "PARTIAL BY CONSTRUCTION. The change filter is '^cartridges/.*/ffi/', so it builds only the FFI of cartridges a PR touched. It never builds an adapter and never sweeps the whole tree. Installs zig 0.15.2 while .tool-versions pins 0.15.1."
  - id: "foundry"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/foundry.yml"
    jobs: ["changes", "provision-harness"]
    gating: "hard"
  - id: "governance"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/governance.yml"
    gating: "hard"
    source: "hyperpolymath/standards/.github/workflows/governance-reusable.yml@81dbf2dd854b1444fd6236fa2352474383b2c2b9"
    note: "Enforces the estate TypeScript allowlist via .governance-allowlist."
  - id: "codeql"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/codeql.yml"
    job: "analyze"
    gating: "hard"
  - id: "secret-scanner"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/secret-scanner.yml"
    gating: "hard"
    source: "hyperpolymath/standards/.github/workflows/secret-scanner-reusable.yml@c65436ee3351cd6b0fa14b142938b195efc77586"
  - id: "hypatia-scan"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/hypatia-scan.yml"
    job: "scan"
    gating: "advisory"
    note: "Runs with --exit-zero and `|| true`. Findings NEVER fail the job; they are uploaded as SARIF and commented on the PR. Do not read a green hypatia-scan as a clean scan. The Hypatia scanner itself is cloned from main, not pinned."
  - id: "scorecard"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/scorecard.yml"
    gating: "advisory"
    source: "hyperpolymath/standards/.github/workflows/scorecard-reusable.yml@81dbf2dd854b1444fd6236fa2352474383b2c2b9"
  - id: "build"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/build.yml"
    job: "sonarqube"
    gating: "advisory"
    note: "SonarCloud quality gate."
  - id: "mirror"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/mirror.yml"
    gating: "non-gating"
    source: "hyperpolymath/standards/.github/workflows/mirror-reusable.yml@d135b05bfc647d0c0fbfedc7e80f37ea50f49236"
    note: "Publishes to other git forges; runs on push to main only."
  - id: "pages"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/pages.yml"
    jobs: ["build", "deploy"]
    gating: "non-gating"
  - id: "pages-deploy"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/pages-deploy.yml"
    job: "deploy"
    gating: "non-gating"
    note: "Cloudflare Pages."
  - id: "push-email-notify"
    workflow: ".github/workflows/push-email-notify.yml"
    job: "notify"
    gating: "non-gating"

untracked_workflow_warning: |
  .github/workflows/main-estate-audit.yml exists in the working tree but is
  NOT tracked in git as of 2026-08-07. It calls 26 hyperpolymath/cicd-suite
  actions, every one pinned to @main rather than to a SHA. It is listed here
  so it is not mistaken for a gate that runs, and so that committing it
  as-is is a conscious decision rather than an accident.

---
### [KNOWN_GAPS]
# Recorded, not papered over. Each is real and reproducible today.
gaps:
  - id: "adapters-do-not-build"
    severity: "high"
    detail: "None of the 99 cartridges/*/adapter/build.zig trees compiles. The gossamer template adapter calls ffi.gossamer_init, which does not exist, and the ffi `export fn` declarations are not `pub`, so the adapter cannot import them. Every minted adapter inherits the fault, so `just mint` output must not be treated as green."
  - id: "adapters-are-ungated"
    severity: "high"
    detail: "No CI job builds any adapter. zig-test.yml filters on '^cartridges/.*/ffi/' only. This is why adapters-do-not-build survived undetected."
  - id: "no-full-tree-sweep"
    severity: "medium"
    detail: "Nothing builds the whole tree. CI builds only what a PR touched, so a cartridge can rot indefinitely as long as nobody edits it."
  - id: "shim-drift-undetected"
    severity: "medium"
    detail: "116 vendored shim copies, 1 divergent, nothing comparing them."
  - id: "empty-abi-dirs"
    severity: "low"
    detail: "18 of 126 abi/ directories contain no .idr file. The proof gate's vacuous-pass guard is whole-run; an individually empty abi/ passes silently."
  - id: "toolchain-pin-disagreement"
    severity: "low"
    detail: ".tool-versions pins zig 0.15.1; zig-test.yml installs 0.15.2."

