### [KNOWN_DRIFT]
known_drift:
  inventory: "audits/cartridge-schema-2026-06-01.md"
  status: "cleared 2026-06-01"
  remediation_tracking:
    - "boj-server-cartridges#18 — category drift — CLOSED"
    - "boj-server-cartridges#19 — auth.method enum drift — CLOSED (canonical side; consumer-side tracked at boj-server#183)"
    - "boj-server-cartridges#20 — missing fields + name-pattern renames — CLOSED"
    - "boj-server-cartridges#29 — shim build-path — CLOSED (97 build.zigs rewritten via #31)"
    - "boj-server-cartridges#32 — browser-mcp error_recover regression — CLOSED (fix bundled into #31)"
  text_corruption_2026_08_07: |
    A global find/replace of "v" -> "zig" corrupted ~140 cartridge READMEs
    and .machine_readable/6a2/PLAYBOOK.a2ml, rewriting the estate's V-lang
    ban notes into claims that ZIG is banned. Corrected on branch
    docs/machine-readable-repair. The corrupted rows also documented
    SIDELINED-*.v.adoc files that exist nowhere in this repository or its
    history; those rows were removed rather than reworded. Regression
    guards: the no-v-zig-substitution-corruption and
    no-phantom-sidelined-files checks in
    .machine_readable/contractiles/Mustfile.a2ml.
